      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Recently, transfection of cis-element double stranded (ds) oligodeoxynucleotides (ODN) (= decoy) as a new powerful tool in a new class of anti-gene strategy for gene therapy and the study of transcriptional regulation has been reported. Transfection of ds ODN corresponding to cis sequence will result in the attenuation of authentic cis-trans interaction, leading to the removal of trans-factors from the endogenous cis-element with subsequent modulation of gene expression. Recent studies provide evidence of on in vivo application of this novel molecular approach as a therapeutic strategy against cardiovascular disease, and tool for the study of gene regulation in vivo."},
